@page
@model ConnectModel

<div class="mb-4">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-1">Connect an IDE</h1>
    <p class="text-body-secondary mb-0">
        Jetpack speaks the JetBrains Marketplace protocol, so IntelliJ-based IDEs (2022.3 and newer)
        use it for the Marketplace tab, plugin updates and dependencies. Pick one of the options below.
    </p>
</div>

@if (Model.ViaMarketplaceName) {
    <div class="alert alert-success d-flex gap-2" role="status">
        @Icons.Render("check")
        <div>
            You reached this page through <strong>plugins.jetbrains.com</strong>, so DNS and the
            certificate are set up correctly on this machine. IDEs here need no further configuration.
        </div>
    </div>
}

<div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-xl-4">
        <div class="card h-100 jp-option jp-option-recommended">
            <div class="card-header d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                @Icons.Render("globe") <span class="fw-semibold">DNS</span>
                <span class="badge bg-primary-subtle text-primary-emphasis ms-auto">Recommended</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>No IDE configuration at all. The stock Marketplace just works.</p>
                <ol class="jp-steps">
                    <li>Resolve <code>plugins.jetbrains.com</code> and <code>downloads.marketplace.jetbrains.com</code>
                        to this server in your internal DNS, for example with dnsmasq:
                        <div class="jp-code mt-2">
                            <pre id="jp-dns"><code>address=/plugins.jetbrains.com/&lt;jetpack-ip&gt;
address=/downloads.marketplace.jetbrains.com/&lt;jetpack-ip&gt;</code></pre>
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm jp-copy" data-jp-copy="#jp-dns" aria-label="Copy">@Icons.Render("copy")</button>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>Serve a TLS certificate for those names (<code>deploy/generate-certs.sh</code> creates one).</li>
                    <li>Install the CA certificate in each developer machine's OS trust store. JetBrains IDEs
                        trust the OS store by default.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Mirrored Marketplace plugins install silently. In-house plugins that aren't signed show a
                    one-time “not signed” prompt in this mode.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-xl-4">
        <div class="card h-100 jp-option">
            <div class="card-header d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                @Icons.Render("terminal") <span class="fw-semibold">VM option</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>Point a single IDE at this server, without changing DNS.</p>
                <ol class="jp-steps">
                    <li>In the IDE open <em>Help | Edit Custom VM Options</em>.</li>
                    <li>Add this line and restart the IDE:
                        <div class="jp-code mt-2">
                            <pre id="jp-vmoption"><code>-Didea.plugins.host=@Model.ServerUrl</code></pre>
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm jp-copy" data-jp-copy="#jp-vmoption" aria-label="Copy">@Icons.Render("copy")</button>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    The certificate must be valid for <code>@Model.ServerHost</code> and trusted on the machine.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-xl-4">
        <div class="card h-100 jp-option">
            <div class="card-header d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
                @Icons.Render("list") <span class="fw-semibold">Custom repository</span>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>The classic plugin repository list. Works with any IDE version.</p>
                <ol class="jp-steps">
                    <li>Open <em>Settings | Plugins | ⚙ | Manage Plugin Repositories</em>.</li>
                    <li>Add:
                        <div class="jp-code mt-2">
                            <pre id="jp-repo"><code>@Model.ServerUrl/updatePlugins.xml</code></pre>
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm jp-copy" data-jp-copy="#jp-repo" aria-label="Copy">@Icons.Render("copy")</button>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Plugins then appear in search results only, next to Marketplace results that fail offline.
                    The old URL <code>/api/plugins/updatePlugins.xml</code> still works.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mt-4">
    <div class="card-header">@Icons.Render("shield") Checking the setup</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <ul class="mb-0">
            <li>Every IDE request is logged by Jetpack with the IDE's name and build, e.g.
                <code>GET /api/search/plugins … (WebStorm/262.11879.105)</code>. No log lines when you open the
                Marketplace tab means DNS or TLS isn't set up yet on that machine.</li>
            <li><em>PKIX path building failed</em> in the IDE: the CA isn't trusted, or the certificate doesn't list
                <code>plugins.jetbrains.com</code>.</li>
            <li>Server status: <a href="/health">/health</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
